      "hit_at_5": true,
      "citation_precision": 1.0,
      "mode": "hybrid",
      "answer": "They selected the sinusoidal version because they hypothesized that its continuous, frequency\u2011based form would make it easy for the model to learn relative positions \u2013 any fixed offset\u202f$k$ can be expressed as a linear function of the encodings at position\u202f$pos$\u202f([2]). This property, together with experiments showing that learned positional embeddings gave almost identical performance, led them to adopt the sinusoidal encoding.",
